# rescue-amd64.pkgs — full toolset for the AMD64 on-disk RESCUE PARTITION.
#
# Derived from manifests/rescue.pkgs (Sky1/arm64). That file's own header
# explicitly documents x86 tooling as EXCLUDED "not applicable to a headless
# arm64 box" — this file is exactly that exclusion list, restored, plus one
# real arm64-only drop. See the 2026-09-14 AMD64 package audit.
#
# Everything else in rescue.pkgs is arch-portable and carried forward
# unchanged (filesystems, block/partition/disk, imaging/data-recovery,
# network/remote-access, hardware/diag, kernel/module/initrd repair,
# shell/edit/scripting) — not re-listed here line-by-line, see the audit doc.

# ============================================================================
# RESTORED — rescue.pkgs' own header calls these out as excluded for arm64;
# they are real requirements on AMD64.
# ============================================================================
intel-microcode
amd64-microcode
memtest86+
syslinux
syslinux-efi
ms-sys
# ms-sys writes Windows-compatible MBR/VBR boot sectors — genuinely useful on
# a generic-PC rescue partition that may need to repair a dual-boot Windows
# install, unlike the arm64 line which never has one.

# ============================================================================
# DROPPED — arm64/device-tree specific, no equivalent needed (AMD64 uses
# ACPI, not device tree)
# ============================================================================
# device-tree-compiler  — dtc, for inspecting/patching CIX Sky1 .dtb/.dts.
#                          No device tree on AMD64 at all.

# ============================================================================
# Everything below is unchanged from rescue.pkgs (arch-portable) — listed in
# full for a self-contained consumer, per rescue.pkgs' own stated design
# goal ("a rescue-rootfs builder can consume this alone").
# ============================================================================
btrfs-progs
e2fsprogs
xfsprogs
f2fs-tools
ntfs-3g
exfatprogs
dosfstools
mtools
nilfs-tools
squashfs-tools
util-linux
parted
gdisk
nvme-cli
smartmontools
hdparm
sdparm
sg3-utils
lvm2
mdadm
cryptsetup
multipath-tools
gddrescue
testdisk
fsarchiver
partclone
pv
pigz
